SUMMARY: The research task is to determine if the series "kv_gb_vs_context_len" supports the claim that sparse attention aids in serving hundred-thousand-token prompts within a memory budget. The web search did not provide specific findings related to the metric series, while the paper search found relevant papers discussing sparse attention and the "kv_gb_vs_context_len" metric in relation to memory budget constraints. The data analysis suggests that the numbers from the "metric_series" indicate a relationship between sparse attention and memory efficiency, but the exact impact on serving hundred-thousand-token prompts is not clearly established. The fact-checking did not provide additional verified information about the "kv_gb_vs_context_len" metric. Overall, while there is some support from the papers that sparse attention can help with memory efficiency, the specific claim about serving hundred-thousand-token prompts within a memory budget is not definitively supported by the available data.
